d 'COPULAENDOG': module to correct endogenous regressors in a linear model when no instrument is available
d
d  copulaendog corrects endogenous regressors in a linear model
d when no instrument is available. The dependence between the
d regressor and the structural error is modelled with a Gaussian
d copula, and the resulting control function is added to the
d regression. Five cross-sectional estimators sit behind one
d interface: Park and Gupta (2012), the two-stage copula generated
d regressor approach of Yang, Qian and Xie (2025), the
d between-regressor correlation variant of Haschka (2025), the
d nonlinear-transformation approach of Breitung, Mayer and Wied
d (2024), and the adjusted estimator of Liengaard et al. (2025).
d Six marginal CDF estimators are available for the copula
d transformation, inference is by pairs bootstrap, and a validity
d option reports the identification requirements the literature
d states — non-normality of the endogenous regressor on both the
d Yang and the Becker criteria, the uncorrelatedness assumption
d where it applies, and the ICON standard-error inflation of Qian,
d Koschmann and Xie (2025). 
d
d KW: endogenity
d KW: copula
d KW: control functions
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260820
d
d Author: Girish Mallapragada,  Kelley School of Business, Indiana University
d Support: email mallapr@@iu.edu
d
f copulaendog.ado
f copulaendog_p.ado
